{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-3398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}I & =\\frac{2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-3398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f1fcd6262e0774cdd29395c7b296578092f541b673d3d21966b1bec378ca347"} {"question" "q-3398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-3398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))}{10}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{10}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{5}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-3398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5})(3{e}^{3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})(3{e}^{3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}(\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{25}-\\frac{9}{25}I \\\\ \\frac{34}{25}I & =\\frac{3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-5{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}{34}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f1fcd6262e0774cdd29395c7b296578092f541b673d3d21966b1bec378ca347"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{34}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{34}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{34}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{3x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}{34}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{3x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}{34}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-12921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{3x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}{34}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{10}{9}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi /3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}))}{10}+\\frac{{e}^{-0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0))}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{-\\pi /3}}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f1fcd6262e0774cdd29395c7b296578092f541b673d3d21966b1bec378ca347"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{-\\pi /3}-5"] ["math" "3{e}^{-\\pi /3}+10"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+3)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}({e}^{-\\pi /3}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-83014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{e}^{-3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-3{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{e}^{-3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-3{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\int {e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3J \\\\ I & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3(-{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-9I \\\\ 10I & ={e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f1fcd6262e0774cdd29395c7b296578092f541b673d3d21966b1bec378ca347"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{10}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-114950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-362667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2}{5}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-362667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by  $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-x})\\,(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-x})\\,(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation for $I,$ we solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}I & =-{e}^{-x}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi /2}}{5}(0-2))-(-\\frac{1}{5}(0+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-\\pi /2}}{5}+\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(1+{e}^{-\\pi /2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a734e9657e1cdeb6aca04fbe019c414f6c92b4a49b28168d8e43"} {"question" "q-362667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f1fcd6262e0774cdd29395c7b296578092f541b673d3d21966b1bec378ca347"} {"question" "q-362667" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068238/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c8e185bb969a